split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புய்த்தெறி","parts":[{"text":"புய்த்து","lemma":"puyttu","gloss":"plucking"},{"text":"எறி","lemma":"eṟi","gloss":"throwing"}],"gloss":"plucking and throwing"},{"surface":"கரும்பின்","parts":[{"text":"கரும்பு","lemma":"karumpu","gloss":"sugarcane"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of sugarcane"},{"surface":"விடுகழை","parts":[{"text":"விடு","lemma":"viṭu","gloss":"discarded"},{"text":"கழை","lemma":"kaḻai","gloss":"stalk"}],"gloss":"discarded stalk"},{"surface":"தாமரைப்","parts":[{"text":"தாமரை","lemma":"tāmarai","gloss":"lotus"},{"text":"ப்","lemma":"p","gloss":"sandhi"}],"gloss":"lotus"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பூம்போது","parts":[{"text":"பூம்போது","lemma":"பூம்போது","gloss":"flower bud"}],"gloss":"flower bud","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"சிதைய","parts":[{"text":"சிதை","lemma":"citai","gloss":"be ruined"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"infinitive marker"}],"gloss":"to be ruined"},{"surface":"வீழ்ந்தெனக்","parts":[{"text":"வீழ்","lemma":"vīḻ","gloss":"fall"},{"text":"ந்து","lemma":"ntu","gloss":"past participle suffix"},{"text":"என","lemma":"eṉa","gloss":"as"},{"text":"க்","lemma":"k","gloss":"sandhi"}],"gloss":"as it fell"},{"surface":"கூத்தர்","parts":[{"text":"கூத்தர்","lemma":"kūttar","gloss":"dancers"}],"gloss":"dancers"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆடுகளம்","parts":[{"text":"ஆடு","lemma":"āṭu","gloss":"dance"},{"text":"களம்","lemma":"kaḷam","gloss":"stage"}],"gloss":"dance stage"},{"surface":"கடுக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"கடு","lemma":"kaṭu","gloss":"resemble"},{"text":"க்கும்","lemma":"kkum","gloss":"resembling"}],"gloss":"resembling"},{"surface":"அகநாட்டையே","parts":[{"text":"அகநாட்டையே","lemma":"அகநாட்டையே","gloss":"the interior country indeed"}],"gloss":"the interior country indeed","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அதனால்","parts":[{"text":"அது","lemma":"atu","gloss":"that"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"aṉ","gloss":"oblique marker"},{"text":"ஆல்","lemma":"āl","gloss":"by"}],"gloss":"therefore"},{"surface":"அறனும்","parts":[{"text":"அறன்","lemma":"aṟaṉ","gloss":"virtue"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and virtue"},{"surface":"பொருளும்","parts":[{"text":"பொருள்","lemma":"poruḷ","gloss":"wealth"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and wealth"},{"surface":"இன்பமும்","parts":[{"text":"இன்பம்","lemma":"iṉpam","gloss":"pleasure"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and pleasure"},{"surface":"மூன்றும்","parts":[{"text":"மூன்று","lemma":"mūṉṟu","gloss":"three"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"all three"}],"gloss":"all three"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆற்றும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆற்று","lemma":"āṟṟu","gloss":"achieve"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"habitual relative participle"}],"gloss":"which achieves"},{"surface":"பெரும","parts":[{"text":"பெரும","lemma":"பெரும","gloss":"O great lord"}],"gloss":"O great lord","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நின்செல்வம்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"},{"text":"செல்வம்","lemma":"celvam","gloss":"wealth"}],"gloss":"your wealth"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆற்றாமை","parts":[{"text":"ஆற்று","lemma":"āṟṟu","gloss":"achieve"},{"text":"ஆமை","lemma":"āmai","gloss":"inability"}],"gloss":"inability to achieve"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"போற்றாமையே","parts":[{"text":"போற்று","lemma":"pōṟṟu","gloss":"protect"},{"text":"ஆமை","lemma":"āmai","gloss":"failure"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"failure to protect indeed"}]}],"literal":"Without excellence blind, without limbs lifeless lump, / hunchback, dwarf, mute, deaf, / animal-like, mentally deranged, including, to those who live, / eight types of defects, these all, / are folly other than benefit is not, thus, / even before those who knew said, even now, / its nature indeed I came to speak. / Round, striped, red-spotted rooster, / which awakened those who guard the millet field, crows / in the forest, such are your enemies; you indeed, / for the people in the outer suburbs, intending charity, those inside / plucked and threw sugarcane's discarded stalks, lotus / flower buds to be ruined fell, as if dancers' / dance stage resembling interior country indeed. / Therefore, virtue, wealth, and pleasure, all three, / which achieves, O great lord, is your wealth; / inability to achieve is your failure to protect indeed.","translation":"Wise men of the past have said, and even today it is true, that the eight defects of human life—blindness, a lifeless lump of flesh, hunchback, dwarfism, muteness, deafness, animal-like ignorance, and mental derangement—bring only misery and no benefit. I have come to speak of this truth. Your enemies are mere forest-dwellers, awakened only by the crowing of the round, striped, red-spotted wild rooster that alerts the guards of the millet fields. But you rule a fertile inner country where those inside the fortress, intending charity, pluck and throw sugarcane stalks to the people waiting in the outer suburbs; these discarded stalks fall upon and crush the beautiful lotus buds, making the fields resemble a stage where dancers have performed. Therefore, O great lord, your immense wealth is meant to achieve the three goals of life: virtue, wealth, and pleasure. If you fail to achieve them, it is solely due to your own lack of vigilance.","modern":"அறிவு குறைந்த குருடு, உறுப்புகள் இல்லாத தசைப்பிண்டம், கூன், குள்ளம், ஊமை, செவிடு, விலங்குத்தன்மை, பித்து ஆகிய எட்டு வகையான குறைபாடுகளும் மனித வாழ்க்கையில் துன்பத்தைத் தருமே தவிர நன்மையைத் தராது என்று முன்னோர் கூறினர்; இப்போதும் அதுவே உண்மை. அதன் தன்மையை உனக்குக் கூறவே நான் இங்கு வந்தேன். வட்டமான வரிகளையும் சிவந்த புள்ளிகளையும் உடைய காட்டுச்சேவல் கூவி எழுப்ப, தினைப்புனம் காப்போர் விழித்தெழும் காட்டில் வாழ்பவர்கள் உனது பகைவர்கள். ஆனால் நீயோ, கோட்டையின் உள்ளே இருப்பவர்கள் வெளியே இருக்கும் மக்களுக்கு அறம் செய்யக் கருதி, கரும்புகளைப் பிடுங்கி எறிய, அவை தாமரை மலர்களைச் சிதைத்து வீழும் வளமான நாட்டை உடையவன். அந்த வயல்கள் கூத்தர்கள் ஆடும் மேடையைப் போலக் காட்சி தரும். ஆகவே, பெருமானே! உனது செல்வம் அறம், பொருள், இன்பம் ஆகிய மூன்றையும் அடைவதற்கே உதவும். அவற்றை நீ அடையாமல் போனால், அது உனது பராக்கினாலேயே (அலட்சியத்தினாலேயே) ஆகும்.","explanation":"The poet Uṟaiyūr Mutukaṇṇaṉ Cāttaṉār addresses the Chola king Nalaṅkiḷḷi in this poem of wise counsel. He begins by listing the eight physical and mental defects that afflict human existence, emphasizing that life is fragile and full of suffering. He contrasts the king's enemies, who live primitive lives in the forest, with Nalaṅkiḷḷi's prosperous and fertile kingdom. In his land, sugarcane stalks thrown in charity crush lotus flowers, creating a scene like a festive dance stage. The poet advises the king that his vast wealth is meant to fulfill the three supreme goals of life—virtue, wealth, and pleasure—and failing to do so would be a failure of his own vigilance.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}